#: ../../../QualGroup.md:86
msgid "Participation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:88
msgid "There are several ways to participate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:90
msgid ""
"Join discussions on the [LLVM Discourse](https://discourse.llvm.org/) forum, "
"under the \"Community\" category."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:91
msgid ""
"Engage in conversations on the LLVM Community Discord in the [#fusa-qual-wg]"
"(https://discord.com/channels/636084430946959380/1389362444169773117) "
"channel. Note: You need to join the community's [Discord chat server]"
"(https://llvm.org/docs/GettingInvolved.html#discord) first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:92
msgid ""
"Join our monthly sync-up calls. Details on working sessions and meeting "
"minutes are shared on the {doc}`GettingInvolved` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:93
msgid ""
"Contribute ideas, feedback, or patches via GitHub, Discourse, or directly in "
"working documents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:95
msgid "Contribution Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:97
msgid ""
"We understand that most members contribute in a limited capacity due to "
"their primary responsibilities. This initiative is volunteer-driven, and we "
"operate with the following shared principles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:99
msgid ""
"**Acknowledgement of limited bandwidth:** We recognize that no one is "
"working full-time on this group, and participation will vary based on "
"individual availability and priorities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:100
msgid ""
"**Small and consistent contributions are valuable:** We believe that steady "
"ongoing contributions, even if minimal, are crucial for long-term success, "
"as long as there is coordination and respect for each other's time. Even "
"small contributions (e.g., a few hours per month) can significantly advance "
"the group's goals and have an impact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:101
msgid ""
"**Realistic progress expectations:** Given the voluntary nature and no full-"
"time involvement, we expect our progress to be slow. This group was "
"initiated in July 2025. Concrete outcomes in 1-2 years would be considered "
"excellent for this type of cross-company and voluntary collaboration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:102
msgid ""
"**Respect for differing capacities:** We value every member’s engagement, "
"whether large or small, often or sporadically, as it all contributes to the "
"overall effort. Even contributions that may seem small, such as sharing an "
"idea or pointing out a relevant resource, are meaningful and important."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:104
msgid ""
"However, we need a balance between flexibility, structure, and enough "
"organization to move forward together. Thus, to support coordination and "
"clarity, the group distinguishes between **active contributors** and "
"**observers / interested participants**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:106
msgid ""
"**Active contributors** are members who provide regular and substantive "
"contributions to the group’s work. This includes ongoing engagement in at "
"least one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:108
msgid ""
"Participation in sync-ups or asynchronous discussions (via Discord or "
"Discourse),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:109
msgid ""
"Contributions to qualification artifacts, methodologies, documentation, "
"structured reviews, or feedback on proposals and drafts,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:110
msgid ""
"Analysis, research activities, or support for coordination, outreach, or "
"other working tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:112
msgid ""
"Active contribution implies sustained engagement that meaningfully advances "
"the group’s objectives. Participation may be synchronous or asynchronous, "
"depending on availability. Participation status reflects current bandwidth "
"and coordination needs and may be updated during the [biannual membership "
"review](#membership-review)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:114
msgid ""
"**Observers**, or **interested participants** are anyone who follows the "
"group’s work and may participate when availability allows. This is an open "
"status and does not require the [nomination process](#nomination-process) "
"used for active contributors. Observers remain welcome to attend meetings, "
"provide feedback, and contribute at any time. Moreover, observer status does "
"not imply reduced importance or access within the group."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:119
msgid "Membership Criteria"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:121
msgid ""
"Membership in the LLVM Qualification Group is intended for individuals with "
"relevant experience or active engagement in qualification-related efforts. "
"Categories include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:123
msgid "**Individual Contributors**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:125
msgid ""
"Experience in software/tool qualification (e.g., reliability, quality, "
"safety, security); OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:126
msgid "Active involvement in LLVM-related qualification efforts; OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:127
msgid ""
"Significant LLVM contributions related to qualification in the past year "
"(code, discussion, resolving related challenges)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:129
msgid "**Researchers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:131
msgid ""
"Active research, publication, or development of methodologies, frameworks, "
"or tools aimed at improving LLVM quality and reliability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:133
msgid "**Vendor Contacts**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:135
msgid ""
"Represent organizations building or using LLVM-based tools in safety-"
"critical environments; OR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:136
msgid ""
"Require involvement due to organizational role in qualification or "
"compliance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:138
msgid "Nomination Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:140
msgid ""
"Individuals may nominate themselves or be nominated by an existing member. "
"Nominations should:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:142
msgid ""
"Explain the nominee’s background and relevance to qualification efforts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:143
msgid ""
"Be submitted via this form: [Participant Introduction & Membership](https://"
"forms.gle/cE1kHjqkKNtafUrD7)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:144
msgid ""
"Be communicated to an active LLVM Qualification Group member (e.g., on the "
"Discord channel)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:146
msgid ""
"This nomination process applies to becoming an **active contributor**. "
"People who simply wish to follow the group’s work or participate "
"occasionally may do so as observers / interested participants, without a "
"formal nomination process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:150
msgid ""
"Nominations are discussed within the group. If consensus is reached, the "
"nominee is accepted. Otherwise, a majority vote will decide."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:152
msgid "Membership Review"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:154
msgid ""
"To ensure the group remains active and focused, member participation is "
"reviewed every six months. Inactive members may be removed following this "
"review."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:156
msgid ""
"During the biannual membership review, members who have not participated in "
"discussions or provided substantive contributions during the review period "
"will be contacted. After consensus, they may be transitioned to **observer** "
"status to reflect current availability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:158
msgid ""
"This transition is procedural and does not restrict participation. Members "
"may resume **active contributor** status at any time when their engagement "
"increases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:160
msgid "Decision Making"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:162
msgid ""
"The LLVM Qualification Working Group aims to make decisions transparently, "
"collaboratively, and without unnecessary formality. The goal is to maintain "
"efficiency while encouraging broad participation and mutual understanding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:164
msgid ""
"This section describes the lightweight process used to handle proposals and "
"decisions within the group. It may be revised as the group evolves and gains "
"experience."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:166
msgid "Principles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:168
msgid ""
"**Consensus first:** The preferred mode of decision-making is consensus "
"through open discussion (primarily on Discord or during sync-up meetings)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:169
msgid ""
"**Inclusiveness and respect:** All viewpoints are encouraged, and members "
"are expected to contribute constructively toward reaching a shared "
"understanding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:170
msgid ""
"**Transparency:** Discussions leading to a decision should be visible to the "
"group and, whenever appropriate, summarized in public channels (e.g., "
"Discourse meeting notes, Discord channel, documentation updates)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:172
msgid "Consensus and Time Limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:174
msgid ""
"Discussions remain open until a clear consensus emerges, meaning no "
"sustained objections have been raised after reasonable discussion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:176
msgid ""
"To prevent open-ended debates, if no new viewpoints are expressed after an "
"agreed period (e.g., 2 weeks), the moderator (typically the person who "
"started the discussion thread) may take one of the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:178
msgid "**Summarize the apparent consensus** and close the discussion, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:179
msgid ""
"**Postpone the topic** to the next sync-up meeting if the outcome remains "
"unclear, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:180
msgid "**Call for a short vote** to confirm the group’s position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:182
msgid "Voting Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:184
msgid ""
"When consensus cannot be reached or when a clear yes/no decision is needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:186
msgid ""
"The moderator may call for a **simple vote** using emoji reactions on "
"Discord or a similar visible method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:187
msgid ""
"A decision passes if it receives a **majority (>50%)** of votes among "
"**participants who voted.** Non-votes are **not counted** in the total."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:188
msgid ""
"To ensure decisions reflect the collective position of the group, **at least "
"three-quarters of the total core members** must participate in the vote for "
"it to be considered valid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:189
msgid ""
"If results are evenly split **(50/50)**, or if participation falls below "
"this threshold, the topic may be postponed to the next sync-up meeting for "
"further discussion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:191
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:193
msgid ""
"Final decisions should be briefly documented (e.g., in meeting minutes, the "
"corresponding GitHub issue, or Discord discussion thread). Once stable, the "
"resulting policy or outcome may be reflected in this documentation for "
"reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:195
msgid "Working Group artifacts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:197
msgid ""
"The LLVM Qualification Working Group develops and maintains its public "
"artifacts and working materials in the [fusa-qual-wg directory of the llvm-"
"wgs repository](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-wgs/tree/main/fusa-qual-wg)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:201
msgid ""
"**This directory is the central location for the group's technical "
"outputs**, including qualification guidance, documentation templates, "
"analyses, proposals, and other materials related to LLVM tools, libraries, "
"quality, and safety. It also contains supporting documentation from the "
"group's activities and meetings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:207
msgid ""
"The artifacts are developed collaboratively and may have different levels of "
"maturity. Unless stated otherwise, they should be understood as working "
"group materials rather than formally approved LLVM policies, certification "
"evidence, or guarantees of suitability for a particular safety-critical "
"application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:213
msgid ""
"Feedback and contributions are welcome through the standard GitHub review "
"process and the group's public discussion channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:216
msgid "Current Topics & Backlog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:218
msgid ""
"Our working group is actively engaged in discussions about the project's "
"direction and tackling technical challenges. You can find our current "
"discussions, challenges, and the project backlog in the following document: "
"[Backlog](https://docs.google.com/document/"
"d/10YZZ72ba09Ck_OiJaP9C4-7DeUiveaIKTE3IkaSKjzA/edit?usp=sharing)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:223
msgid ""
"This document serves as our central hub for all ongoing topics and will be "
"updated regularly to reflect our progress. We welcome your contributions and "
"feedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:227
msgid "Meeting Materials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:229
msgid ""
"Meeting agendas, minutes, and supporting materials are published to ensure "
"transparency and continuity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:231
msgid ""
"Upcoming and past meeting agendas, and meeting minutes are published in a "
"dedicated thread on the LLVM Discourse forum: [Meeting Agendas and Minutes]"
"(https://discourse.llvm.org/t/llvm-qualification-wg-sync-ups-meeting-"
"minutes/87148)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:234
msgid ""
"Slides used to support discussions during sync-up meetings are stored in a "
"[dedicated Google Drive folder](https://drive.google.com/drive/u/1/"
"folders/1nu3JAanE0gqQDll0S9ofVy4FOFezc6Mm). Note that the naming convention "
"for these slides is *YYYYMM*\\_llvm_qual_wg."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:238
msgid ""
"While Discourse is our active communication channel for agendas and "
"announcements, the `llvm-wgs` repository is our durable, central location "
"for both WG artifacts and meeting records. The [meeting directory in the "
"llvm-wgs repository](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-wgs/tree/main/fusa-qual-wg/"
"meetings) provides the long-term archive of the working group's meeting "
"records. It contains:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:243
msgid ""
"[archived meeting materials](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-wgs/tree/main/fusa-"
"qual-wg/meetings/materials), and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:244
msgid ""
"[archived meeting agendas and minutes](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-wgs/tree/"
"main/fusa-qual-wg/meetings/minutes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:246
msgid "AI Transcription Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:248
msgid "Objective"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:250
msgid ""
"The LLVM Qualification Group may enable AI auto-transcription (currently "
"using Gemini) during sync-up calls in order to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:252
msgid "Make complex discussions easier to follow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:253
msgid "Reduce the effort of manual note-taking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:254
msgid ""
"Support inclusivity for participants who are not native English speakers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:256
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:258
msgid "The purpose of auto-transcripts is to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:260
msgid ""
"Ensure participants can remain engaged during the sync-up meeting "
"(particularly helpful for non-native English speakers or when audio clarity "
"is limited)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:261
msgid ""
"Serve as an aid for preparing the meeting minutes that are published on "
"Discourse: [Meeting Agendas and Minutes](https://discourse.llvm.org/t/llvm-"
"qualification-wg-sync-ups-meeting-minutes/87148)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:264
msgid "Additional safeguards include:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:266
msgid ""
"Transcript files are private to the note-taker(s) and never circulated to "
"attendees or the public."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:267
msgid "Transcript files are permanently deleted once the minutes are posted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:268
msgid ""
"The meeting chair or scribe remains responsible for reviewing the "
"transcript, ensuring accuracy, and editing out sensitive details in the "
"official minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:270
msgid "Vendor Retention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:272
msgid ""
"Long-term storage or model-training settings are disabled on the account "
"used for organizing the working group calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:274
msgid ""
"However, according to Google’s Gemini documentation, even with all history "
"features disabled, voice and transcript data may be retained on Google’s "
"servers for up to ~72 hours for the purpose of \"*keeping Gemini safe and "
"secure, including with help from human reviewers*\" before deletion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:276
msgid "This retention period cannot currently be shortened."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:278
msgid "Consent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:280
msgid ""
"At the start of each sync-up, participants will be asked if they are "
"comfortable with enabling auto-transcription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:281
msgid ""
"If any participant objects, auto-transcription will be disabled for that "
"meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:282
msgid ""
"Participants may also request at any point that parts of the discussion not "
"be transcribed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:284
msgid "Recordings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:286
msgid "Meetings are not recorded by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:287
msgid ""
"Exceptions are made only when explicit approval from attendees is obtained "
"(e.g., for a special-hosted demo)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:289
msgid "Transparency & Feedback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:291
msgid ""
"We want to ensure this practice remains transparent and comfortable for "
"everyone. If any group members have concerns (e.g., about names appearing in "
"transcripts or minutes), they are encouraged to raise them on Discourse or "
"Discord so they can be addressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:293
msgid "Code of Conduct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:295
msgid ""
"We are committed to fostering a respectful, inclusive, and constructive "
"environment where contributors from diverse backgrounds and organizations "
"can collaborate on qualification-related efforts in the LLVM ecosystem. To "
"support this goal, we adopt the following principles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:300
msgid "Let's Build This Together"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:302
msgid ""
"This is a space for shared ownership and mutual learning. If you're here, "
"you belong. Help us shape a group where trust, technical rigor, and "
"collaboration go hand in hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:305
msgid "Respect and Inclusion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:307
msgid ""
"Treat all participants with respect and dignity, regardless of background, "
"experience level, employer, or role in the community."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:308
msgid ""
"Be welcoming and supportive. We value a diversity of opinions and expertise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:309
msgid "Assume good intent, and ask questions before drawing conclusions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:311
msgid "Constructive Collaboration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:313
msgid "Keep discussions focused, technical, and solution-oriented."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:314
msgid ""
"Provide thoughtful, actionable feedback. Avoid sarcasm, dismissive remarks, "
"or personal criticism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:315
msgid ""
"Recognize that contributors have different constraints and priorities. Seek "
"alignment, not perfection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:317
msgid "Transparency and Openness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:319
msgid ""
"Share relevant information openly to enable others to contribute effectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:320
msgid ""
"Document decisions and rationales so others can understand and build on them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:321
msgid ""
"Clearly distinguish between personal opinions, organizational positions, and "
"community consensus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:323
msgid "Unacceptable Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:325
msgid "We will not tolerate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:327
msgid "Harassment, discrimination, or exclusionary behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:328
msgid "Disruptive conduct in meetings or communication channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:329
msgid ""
"Using this group for marketing, lobbying, or promoting non-collaborative "
"commercial agendas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:331
msgid "Safety and Trust"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:333
msgid ""
"We aim to build qualification artifacts that others can trust. Similarly, we "
"aim to be trustworthy collaborators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../QualGroup.md:334
msgid ""
"If you see something concerning, speak up respectfully or contact the group "
"organizer(s) privately."
msgstr ""

